          "question": "I had flu two weeks ago and I am still exhausted. Is prolonged tiredness afterwards a concern, and what does guidance describe about antivirals and vaccination?",
          "answer": "I can't answer the question about lingering tiredness after flu from the guidance I searched. None of the returned passages discuss fatigue after influenza, so I can't say whether it is a concern for you.\n\nThe one relevant source is the **influenza vaccination and antivirals guidance** (National immunization advisory committee and infectious diseases society guidance, educational summary). The passage I received covers annual vaccination. It says that US guidance recommends yearly flu vaccination for everyone aged 6 months and older who has no contraindication, that vaccination before the end of October is the usual aim in the northern hemisphere, and that later vaccination is still worthwhile while the virus circulates. It did not include the section on antiviral timing, so I can't tell you what that guidance says about antivirals.\n\nThe other passages (on asthma, COPD, coronary artery disease and suicidal thoughts) did not address your situation.\n\nThe symptom check found no emergency pattern in your description. That does not rule out a problem. Please contact a doctor or other clinician if your exhaustion is severe, is getting worse, or includes anything new or unexplained. They can look at your symptoms and history, which I can't do.\n\nNot medical advice. This is an educational software project. It does not diagnose or treat, and it must not be used for real medical decisions.",
